    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Difficult terrain is for people who pause.</em></p><p>Your movement speed cannot be reduced below <strong>half your base speed</strong> by any effect, condition, surface, or creature short of a physical barrier substantial enough to stop a charging rhino (GM call). This includes — but is not limited to — difficult terrain, grease, web, the <strong>restrained</strong> condition, the <strong>prone</strong> condition's stand-up cost, slowed/snared effects, and being grappled by a creature your size or smaller.</p><p>You still take damage from traps and hazardous terrain along your path; you simply do not stop for them. You may end movement voluntarily.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
